"USCA Form 1 (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/form29.pdf)\nciteturn1448view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view0\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 20\nL0@P0: UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS\nL1@P0: FOR THE NINTH CIRCUIT\nL2@P0: Form 29. Request for Docket Sheet, Document, or Rules\nL3@P0: Instructions for this form: http://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/forms/form29instructions.pdf\nL4@P0: 9th Cir. Case Number(s)\nL5@P0: Case Name\nL6@P0: What are you requesting?\nL7@P0: A copy of the Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure and 9th Circuit Rules\nL8@P0: A copy of the 9th Circuit docket sheet\nL9@P0: A copy of the following document(s) on the 9th Circuit docket:\nL10@P0: Date and/or Docket Entry # Description of Document\nL11@P0: Your Name\nL12@P0: Your mailing address\nL13@P0: City State Zip Code\nL14@P0: Prisoner Inmate or A Number (if applicable)\nL15@P0: Signature Date\nL16@P0: Mail this form to the court at:\nL17@P0: Clerk, U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, P.O. Box 193939, San Francisco, CA 94119-3939\nL18@P0: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL19@P0: Form 29 New 12/01/2018\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSCA Form 1 (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/form30.pdf)\nciteturn1448view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view1\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 27\nL0@P0: UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS\nL1@P0: FOR THE NINTH CIRCUIT\nL2@P0: Form 30. Appellate Electronic Filing Exemption Form\nL3@P0: ATTENTION SELF-REPRESENTED PARTIES:\nL4@P0: DO NOT USE FORM 30\nL5@P0: If you do not have a lawyer, you are automatically exempt from electronic filing.\nL6@P0: 9th Cir. Case Number(s)\nL7@P0: Case Name\nL8@P0: I am a court reporter\nL9@P0: I am counsel of record for\nL10@P0: (party/parties that you represent)\nL11@P0: I hereby request an exemption from the court's requirement that all attorneys and\nL12@P0: court reporters use Appellate Electronic Filing. I am unable to register for\nL13@P0: electronic filing because:\nL14@P0: My name is\nL15@P0: Mailing address\nL16@P0: City State Zip Code\nL17@P0: Country (if not USA) Phone\nL18@P0: If approved, I understand that this exemption will apply to all pending and future\nL19@P0: cases in this court for one calendar year. If I wish to participate in Appellate\nL20@P0: Electronic Filing in the future, my Appellate Electronic Filing registration will\nL21@P0: apply to all pending and future cases.\nL22@P0: Signature Date\nL23@P0: Mail this form to the court at:\nL24@P0: Clerk, U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, P.O. Box 193939, San Francisco, CA 94119-3939\nL25@P0: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL26@P0: Form 30 Rev. 12/01/2018\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSCA Form 1 (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/form31.pdf)\nciteturn1448view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view2\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 64\nL0@P0: UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS\nL1@P0: FOR THE NINTH CIRCUIT\nL2@P0: Form 31. Application and Oath for Admission\nL3@P0: Instructions for this form: http://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/content/atty_instructions.php\nL4@P0: PERSONAL INFORMATION\nL5@P0: Full Name:\nL6@P0: Last 4 digits of SSN: Birth Date:\nL7@P0: Phone: Email:\nL8@P0: MAILING ADDRESS (no P.O. Box addresses)\nL9@P0: Firm Name or Agency:\nL10@P0: Street Address, incl. Suite/Apt #:\nL11@P0: City: State: Zip:\nL12@P0: BAR INFORMATION\nL13@P0: Federal/State Admissions\nL14@P0: (max. 2)\nL15@P0: Status\nL16@P0: (active/inactive)\nL17@P0: Admission\nL18@P0: Date Bar Number\nL19@P0: Answer each question below. If the answer to any of the questions is yes, attach a\nL20@P0: separate statement providing details.\nL21@P0: 1. Have you been known by any name other than that appearing\nL22@P0: on the application?\nL23@P0: Yes No\nL24@P0: 2. Have you ever been reprimanded, or suspended or disbarred\nL25@P0: from practice, before any court or government agency?\nL26@P0: Yes No\nL27@P0: 3. Are any actions concerning possible reprimand, suspension, or\nL28@P0: disbarment currently pending against you?\nL29@P0: Yes No\nL30@P0: 4. Are you currently under investigation by any court or\nL31@P0: government agency?\nL32@P0: Yes No\nL33@P0: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL34@P0-1: Form 31 1 Rev. 12/01/2018SPONSORED MOTION FOR ADMISSION ONLY\nL35@P1: To be completed by a sponsor in good standing with the Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals\nL36@P1: (Skip to the next section if you were sworn in at a mass bar admission ceremony\nL37@P1: within the last three (3) months.)\nL38@P1: I, , a member in good standing of the\nL39@P1: Bar of the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit hereby move the\nL40@P1: admission of to the Bar of this Court.\nL41@P1: I am satisfied that the applicant possesses the qualifications set forth by Federal\nL42@P1: Rule of Appellate Procedure 46(a).\nL43@P1: (full name of sponsor)\nL44@P1: Sponsor Signature: Date:\nL45@P1: Admission Date:\nL46@P1: Phone: Email:\nL47@P1: Firm Name or Agency:\nL48@P1: Street Address, incl. Suite/Apt #:\nL49@P1: City: State: Zip:\nL50@P1: INFORMATION FOR MASS ADMISSION CEREMONY ONLY\nL51@P1: Location of Ceremony:\nL52@P1: Date of Ceremony:\nL53@P1: OATH\nL54@P1: I, , certify under penalty of perjury\nL55@P1: under the laws of the United States of America that the foregoing is true and\nL56@P1: correct. I do solemnly swear [or affirm] that I will conduct myself as an attorney\nL57@P1: and counselor of this Court, uprightly and according to law; and that I will support\nL58@P1: the Constitution of the United States.\nL59@P1: (TYPE name as you want it to appear on your certificate)\nL60@P1: Applicant Signature Date\nL61@P1: (use “s/[typed name]” to sign electronically-filed documents)\nL62@P1: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL63@P1: Form 31 2 Rev. 12/01/2018\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSCA Form 1 (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/form32.pdf)\nciteturn1448view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view3\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 20\nL0@P0: UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS\nL1@P0: FOR THE NINTH CIRCUIT\nL2@P0: Form 32. Response to Notice of Case Being Considered for Oral Argument\nL3@P0: Instructions for this form: http://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/forms/form32instructions.pdf\nL4@P0: 9th Cir. Case Number(s)\nL5@P0: Case Name\nL6@P0: Hearing Location (city)\nL7@P0: Your Name\nL8@P0: List the sitting dates for the two sitting months you were asked to review:\nL9@P0: Do you have an irreconcilable conflict on any of the above dates? No\nL10@P0: If yes, list the specific day(s) and the specific reason(s) you are unavailable:\nL11@P0: Do you have any other cases pending in this court for which you received a notice\nL12@P0: of consideration for oral argument during the three sitting months listed above?\nL13@P0: Yes No\nL14@P0: If yes, list the number, name, and hearing city of each of the other case(s):\nL15@P0: Signature Date\nL16@P0: (use “s/[typed name]” to sign electronically-filed documents)\nL17@P0: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL18@P0: Form 32 Rev 4/06/2026\nL19@P0: Yes\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/form34.pdf)\nciteturn1448view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view4\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 54\nL0@P0: Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL1@P0: Form 34 1 New 12/01/24\nL2@P0: UNITED STATES COURT OF APPEALS\nL3@P0: FOR THE NINTH CIRCUIT\nL4@P0: Form 34. Disclosure Statement under FRAP 26.1 and Circuit Rule 26.1-1\nL5@P0: Instructions for this form: http://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/forms/form34instructions.pdf\nL6@P0: 9th Cir. Case Number(s) _____________________________________________\nL7@P0: Name(s) of party/parties, prospective intervenor(s), or amicus/amici filing this form:\nL8@P0: Under FRAP 26.1 and Circuit Rule 26.1-1, I make the following disclosures:\nL9@P0: 1. I disclose the following information required by FRAP 26.1(a) and/or Circuit\nL10@P0: Rule 26.1-1(b) for any nongovernmental corporation, association, joint venture,\nL11@P0: partnership, limited liability company, or similar entity1 which is a party,\nL12@P0: prospective intervenor, or amicus curiae in any proceeding, or which the\nL13@P0: government identifies as an organizational victim below in section 2 of this\nL14@P0: form,2\nL15@P0:  or which is a debtor as disclosed below in section 3 of this form.\nL16@P0: a. Does the party, prospective intervenor, amicus, victim, or debtor have any\nL17@P0: parent companies? Parent companies include all companies that control the\nL18@P0: entity directly or indirectly through intermediaries.\nL19@P0: [ ] Yes [ ] No\nL20@P0: If yes, identify all parent corporations of each entity, including all\nL21@P0: generations of parent corporations (attach additional pages as necessary):\nL22@P0: b. Is 10% or more of the stock of the party, prospective intervenor, amicus,\nL23@P0: victim, or debtor owned by a publicly held corporation or other publicly\nL24@P0: held entity?\nL25@P0: [ ] Yes [ ] No\nL26@P0: 1 A corporate entity must be identified by its full corporate name as registered with a secretary of\nL27@P0: state’s office and, if its stock is publicly listed, its stock symbol or “ticker.”\nL28@P0-1: 2 To the extent it can be obtained through due diligence.Feedback or questions about this form? Email us at forms@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL29@P1: Form 34 2 New 12/01/24\nL30@P1: If yes, identify all such owners for each entity (attach additional pages as\nL31@P1: necessary):\nL32@P1: 2. In a criminal case, absent good cause shown, the government must identify here\nL33@P1: any organizational victim of the alleged criminal activity:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/form-35-cir-rule-46-5-exemption.pdf)\nciteturn1448view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view5\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 20\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1448view6 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view6\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/Informal-Opening-Brief-Form-Appeals.pdf)\nciteturn1448view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 6; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view7\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 57\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/Informal-Reply-Brief-Form-Appeals.pdf)\nciteturn1448view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1435view8\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 29\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/uploads/forms/student_practice_forms/Certification%20for%20Law%20Student%20Representation.pdf)\nciteturn1448view9 [wordli